  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0002 database is used to store information about users, data types, menus, menu items, roles, settings, permissions, permission roles, translations, data rows, and user roles. The users table contains information about each user, including their ID, avatar, role ID, and settings. The data types table contains information about each data type, including its ID, name, slug, display name singular and plural, icon, model name, policy name, controller, description, generate permissions, server side, details, created at, and updated at. The menus table contains information about each menu, including its ID, name, created at, and updated at. The menu items table contains information about each menu item, including its ID, menu ID, title, URL, target, icon class, color, parent ID, order, created at, updated at, route, parameters, and foreign keys to the menu items and menus tables. The roles table contains information about each role, including its ID, name, display name, created at, and updated at. The settings table contains information about each setting, including its ID, key, display name, value, details, type, order, and group. The permissions table contains information about each permission, including its ID, key, table name, created at, and updated at. The permission roles table contains information about each permission role, including its permission ID and role ID, and foreign keys to the permissions and roles tables. The translations table contains information about each translation, including its ID, table name, column name, foreign key, locale, value, created at, and updated at. The data rows table contains information about each data row, including its ID, data type ID, field, type, display name, required, browse, read, edit, add, delete, details, and order, and foreign keys to the data types table. The user roles table contains information about each user role, including its user ID and role ID, and foreign keys to the roles and users tables.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nVoyager is an admin panel package for Laravel, developed by The Control Group. It provides a rapid scaffolding solution for backend management, simplifying common administrative tasks within Laravel applications. The package is designed to enhance usability for developers by offering pre-built functionalities for managing app data and user interfaces, thereby reducing development time and effort.\n\n Objectives\n\nThe primary objective of Voyager is to streamline the development of admin interfaces for Laravel applications. It aims to provide:\n- A cohesive admin interface for managing application data.\n- Easily configurable tools for creating and handling BREAD/CRUD operations.\n- Efficient media and menu management functionalities.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Developers: Primary users who integrate Voyager into their Laravel applications to manage backend admin tasks.\n- Admin Users: Users who access the admin panel to perform data management, media handling, and menu building.\n- The Control Group: Developers and maintainers of the Voyager package.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n\n1. Admin Interface: Allows users to add, edit, and delete app data. \n2. Menu Builder: Facilitates creation and management of site menus, allowing for the addition, editing, and deletion of items across various menu locations such as header, sidebar, and footer.\n3. Media Manager: Provides capabilities for uploading, renaming, and deleting files. Users can also create and organize folders.\n4. CRUD/BREAD Builder: Enables the generation of CRUD operations and BREAD functionalities across application tables. \n5. User Roles and Permissions: Manages user roles and permissions to access different admin functionalities.\n6. Data Type Management: Supports defining and managing different data types and their attributes.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Performance: The admin panel should handle operations efficiently to ensure a smooth user experience without unnecessary delays.\n- Scalability: The system should support scaling as the application data and user base grow.\n- Security: All data interactions and file management operations should be secured to prevent unauthorized access and data breaches.\n- Usability: The interface should be intuitive and easy for both developers and admin users to navigate and operate.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0002.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0002\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `avatar` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `settings` json DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `users_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `data_types` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `display_name_singular` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `display_name_plural` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `icon` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `model_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `policy_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `controller` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `generate_permissions` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `server_side` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `details` json DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `menus` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `menu_items` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `menu_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `target` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `icon_class` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `color` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `parent_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `order` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `route` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `parameters` json DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `menu_items_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`menu_id`) REFERENCES `menus` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `menu_items_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`parent_id`) REFERENCES `menu_items` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `roles` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `display_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `settings` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `key` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `display_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `value` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `details` json DEFAULT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `order` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `group` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `permissions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `key` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `table_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `permission_roles` (\n  `permission_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`permission_id`, `role_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `permission_roles_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`permission_id`) REFERENCES `permissions` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `permission_roles_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `translations` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `table_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `column_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `foreign_key` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `locale` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `value` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `data_rows` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `data_type_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `field` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `display_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `required` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `browse` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `read` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `edit` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `add` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `delete` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `details` json DEFAULT NULL,\n  `order` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `data_rows_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`data_type_id`) REFERENCES `data_types` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_roles` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `role_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_roles_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_roles_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
